/** @mainpage Qore ocr Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section ocrintro ocr Module Introduction

    The \c ocr module provides text extraction from images using the Tesseract
    OCR engine.  It supports PNG, JPEG, TIFF, BMP, and GIF input formats and
    returns extracted text along with confidence scores and bounding-box
    metadata.

    Classes provided by this module:
    - @ref Qore::Ocr::TesseractEngine "TesseractEngine" — Tesseract OCR
      engine wrapper

    @section ocrsandboxing Sandboxing

    OCR with the system data directory, used when no data directory is given to
    @ref Qore::Ocr::TesseractEngine::constructor() "TesseractEngine::constructor()", needs no filesystem access rights,
    so it is available to programs with the \c PO_NO_FILESYSTEM restriction.  An explicit data directory is read on
    behalf of the calling program: it needs filesystem access rights, and with a filesystem sandbox, each trained data
    file Tesseract loads must be allowed by the sandbox and may only configure layout, segmentation and recognition
    parameters, so that trained data cannot make Tesseract read or write any other file.

    @section ocrqlibmodules Qore User Modules

    - @ref qoreocrutilsintro "QoreOcrUtils" — OCR support with native Tesseract and HTTP backends, plus scanned PDF detection

    @par Documentation

    - @anchor ocr_relnotes @subpage ocrreleasehistory

*/
